msgid "it.book.cid.name"
msgstr "The Song of My Cid"

msgid "it.book.cid.desc"
msgstr "Homage and oath. Those who hear it hesitate before striking."

msgid "it.book.tio_andalus.name"
msgstr "The Tale of the Uncle from Andalus"

msgid "it.book.tio_andalus.desc"
msgstr "A house that smells of blood. The cellar door is not where it should be."

msgid "it.book.celestina.name"
msgstr "Celestina"

msgid "it.book.celestina.desc"
msgstr "Every thread is a rope, and every rope is in her hand."

msgid "it.ability.desvelar.name"
msgstr "Unveil"

msgid "it.ability.desvelar.desc"
msgstr "Strip the book-skin from a thing and see what it truly is."

msgid "it.ability.refutar.name"
msgstr "Refute"

msgid "it.ability.refutar.desc"
msgstr "Deny what the world claims. For a moment, it must listen."

msgid "it.ability.juramento.name"
msgstr "The Oath"

msgid "it.ability.juramento.desc"
msgstr "Those who made a vow once do not break it easily."

msgid "it.ability.dodge.name"
msgstr "Dodge"

msgid "it.ability.dodge.desc"
msgstr "A step to the side, and the blow goes past."

msgid "dia.sancho.bark.001"
msgstr "By all the saints, it's a mill."

msgid "dia.sancho.bark.002"
msgstr "Master, they're only stones and wood."

msgid "dia.quixote.bark.001"
msgstr "Woe upon you, mortal beast! I will cleave you from your shoulders!"

msgid "dia.quixote.bark.002"
msgstr "I know your kind. I know the mischief you have done in the world."

# --- B5: THE REACTIONS -----------------------------------------------------
# The line a character says when the world moves under them. The key is
# composed: dia.<character>.reaction.<thing>.<book|reality>. "book" is the
# reading they have just arrived at, not the one they left.

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the windmill as a giant.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.windmill.book"
msgstr "A giant! Look at it, a giant! There is no wind in my books!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the windmill as a windmill again.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.windmill.reality"
msgstr "Ah. A windmill. Only a windmill. Forgive me, Sancho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the rock as a book.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.rock.book"
msgstr "A book! Look, a book! Who put it here?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the rock as a rock again.
#. It must NOT name the other truth: the Book reaction is subtle, and
#. this one has to be as subtle as that one. The playtest called the old
#. wording a dead giveaway.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.rock.reality"
msgstr "A stone. Only a stone. Forgive me."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the windmill as a giant.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.windmill.book"
msgstr "Er... that mill has gone giant."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the windmill as a windmill again.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.windmill.reality"
msgstr "There it is. A mill, as always."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the rock as a book.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.rock.book"
msgstr "The stone has turned into a book, master."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the rock as a rock again.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.rock.reality"
msgstr "A stone. Only a stone."

#. TRANSLATORS: The prompt under the examination, when it is open: E
#. closes it again.
msgid "ui.examine.close"
msgstr "E - Close"

# --- THE CHATTER (B3) ---------------------------------------------------
# What the companion says about the thing it is looking at. The key is
# composed: dia.<character>.chatter.<thing>.

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, looking at the rock. He is formal, and a little mad.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.rock"
msgstr "A stone, Sancho... though by tomorrow it may be a book again, and rightly so."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, looking at the windmill.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.windmill"
msgstr "Mills, Sancho. And giants, if the wind is in the mood for giants."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, looking at the training dummy. He will call it a giant.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.dummy"
msgstr "A dummy, Sancho. A wooden giant, if you would have it so."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, when the player locks onto something.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.locked"
msgstr "At the giant, Sancho! Do you see it? It moves on its own. To battle!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, when the player goes down.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.down"
msgstr "Get up, Sancho! It is not your fault: the stone was badly placed."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, with nothing in front of him. Line 1 of 3.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.idle.1"
msgstr "The plain says nothing, Sancho. Not even she does."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, with nothing in front of him. Line 2 of 3.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.idle.2"
msgstr "And to think that from here to a castle — no, a mill, we shall have seen a castle."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, with nothing in front of him. Line 3 of 3.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.idle.3"
msgstr "Silence, Sancho. It is the silence before a battle."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, looking at the rock. Plain, practical, not impressed.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.rock"
msgstr "A stone, your lordship. The sort there are plenty of."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, looking at the windmill.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.windmill"
msgstr "A mill, your lordship. The usual sort: stone and wind."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, looking at the training dummy. He knows what it is.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.dummy"
msgstr "A dummy, your lordship. Put there to be hit."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, when the player locks onto something.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.locked"
msgstr "Ah, are we going for it, your lordship? Oh, but nobody moves it."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, when the player goes down.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.down"
msgstr "Get up, they are hitting you! And get out of the way!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, with nothing in front of him. Line 1 of 3.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.idle.1"
msgstr "This place is quieter than your Rocinante, your lordship."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, with nothing in front of him. Line 2 of 3.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.idle.2"
msgstr "Not a soul here, your lordship. Not one of the kind that looks for trouble."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, with nothing in front of him. Line 3 of 3.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.idle.3"
msgstr "At this rate we will reach the inn before dark."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, after a parry. He cannot parry, so this line is
#. only ever heard if the character who is driving is Sancho.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.parry"
msgstr "There! I have him! Right on the nose, Sancho!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, after a parry.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.parry"
msgstr "I caught that one, your lordship! Did you see?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, after a Desvelar: he has stripped the Book skin
#. off a thing and both of them can see what is under it.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.desvelar"
msgstr "There is the truth of it, your lordship! Look at it. Look well."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, when the Venture of Montiel has fallen.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.venture_down"
msgstr "The giant is down, Sancho! The mill stands as it was, a mill again."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, when the Venture of Montiel has fallen.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.venture_down"
msgstr "The mill stands again, your lordship. The giant is no more."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, with nothing in front of him. Line 4 of 6.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.idle.4"
msgstr "The wind stirs, Sancho. Something is coming."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, with nothing in front of him. Line 5 of 6.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.idle.5"
msgstr "I could spend a lifetime watching these plains."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote, with nothing in front of him. Line 6 of 6.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.idle.6"
msgstr "Even the stones have stories, Sancho. You need only ask them."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, with nothing in front of him. Line 4 of 6.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.idle.4"
msgstr "The sun is climbing, your lordship. Best we keep moving."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, with nothing in front of him. Line 5 of 6.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.idle.5"
msgstr "I could do with some shade, your lordship. And perhaps a snack."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho, with nothing in front of him. Line 6 of 6.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.idle.6"
msgstr "This land is vast, your lordship. And mostly empty."

msgid "tip.lectura.intro"
msgstr "Hold on to the page. Some things only show themselves to a patient eye."

msgid "tip.switch.intro"
msgstr "Change companion. The world is the same; only the reading differs."

msgid "tip.posada.intro"
msgstr "Rest, and the road will still be there."

# --- BOOK LAYER -------------------------------------------------------
# The 1605 original is CONTENT and stays in Spanish in every build. It lives in
# assets/manifiesto/*.json. Only the ".modern" strings are translated.

msgid "bk.ch08.molinos.01.modern"
msgstr ""
"And there appeared to him some thirty or forty monstrous mills that stand "
"on the plain, and so great and tall that they cover the millraces, and "
"the sails of them, going round, made such a din that it seemed as if the "
"winds were grinding the wheat there."

msgid "bk.ch23.montesinos.01.modern"
msgstr ""
"And he told him how he had found a certain enchanted cave in that place, "
"and how a knight came out of it, and how he was leaving him now to go and "
"seek him."

msgid "bk.ch26.galimatias.01.modern"
msgstr ""
"It must be one of three things: the widow is in love with the youth, and "
"the youth with the maiden, and the maiden with neither."

msgid "bk.ch50.impertinente.01.modern"
msgstr ""
"For the tale of the Curious Impertinent is the one I would have written, "
"were it not that my pen is not so bold as to paint the charm of the love "
"that was in it."

