msgid "ui.slice.line.venture"
msgstr "%s: %d/%d"

#. TRANSLATORS: The move the Venture is winding up. Format: %s.
msgid "ui.slice.line.venture.move"
msgstr "preparing: %s"

#. TRANSLATORS: The Venture of Montiel is over.
msgid "ui.slice.venture.down"
msgstr "The mill of Montiel has fallen."

#. TRANSLATORS: The Venture of Montiel is over — resolved by truth, not force.
#. The knight's delusion held: the world stayed Book, the giant was real,
#. and a fragment of the original book is granted.
msgid "ui.slice.venture.truth"
msgstr "The mill of Montiel stands — as a giant."

#. TRANSLATORS: The codex note on the Venture in its Reality form.
msgid "ui.codex.venture.mill"
msgstr "The mill of Montiel in its true shape: stone, grain, and a low door you can walk in through."

#. TRANSLATORS: The codex note on the Venture in its Book form.
msgid "ui.codex.venture.giant"
msgstr "The giant of the mills of Montiel in the Book's shape: the man in the mill, and not the stone."

#. TRANSLATORS: The companion, remarking on the Venture.
msgid "dia.quixote.chatter.venture"
msgstr "A mill! Sancho, a real mill, with its stone and its grain. Do not touch it, for it defends itself."

#. TRANSLATORS: The companion, remarking on the Venture.
msgid "dia.sancho.chatter.venture"
msgstr "That mill, my lord, grinds no grain. It is coming towards us."

#. TRANSLATORS: The character says so when the world shows them a mill.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.venture.reality"
msgstr "Now it is a mill. Stone and wind and grain, and nothing else."

#. TRANSLATORS: The character says so when the world shows them a giant.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.venture.book"
msgstr "That mill is a giant! A giant with arms of stone! Stand back, Sancho, he is coming."

#. TRANSLATORS: The character says so when the world shows them a mill.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.venture.reality"
msgstr "Ah. A mill. So that is what it was."

#. TRANSLATORS: The character says so when the world shows them a giant.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.venture.book"
msgstr "My lord! The mill is a man! A man with sails for arms!"

